      "id": "claim_14ef64f29ae94aac87b6973ce50f2b0f",
      "statement": "A Generation is everything a node derives from a deployment (compiled Worker configs, isolate pools, the Durable Object class registry, the service-binding graph, asset resolvers, cron schedule); a node serves exactly one current generation and reaches it through a snapshot, and boot and reload build through the same two functions.",
